\import{swarm-macros}

\title{Weeknotes for 7 November 2026 (week 44)}
\date{2026-11-07}
\tag{weeknote}

\put\transclude/numbered{false}

\subtree{
  \title{Politics}

  \p{I usually stay away from writing about politics.  But I am of course quite pleased at the results of this week's midterm elections in the US.  Everyone knows about the \em{national} results; but there is good news at the hyper-local level as well.  For the last two years my wife has served as a "Justice of the Peace" on [our county's "Quorum Court"](https://www.faulknercountyar.gov/quorum-court/)—basically a body of elected officials who are responsible for overseeing the county budget.  A lot of it is mundane, but every now and then there are more consequential issues at stake (data centers, ICE funding, \etc). She ran unopposed and was re-elected, which was unremarkable (though still worth celebrating).  However, three more out of the 13 seats flipped from Republican to Democrat (one by a razor-thin margin of 5 votes!), for a total of 5 Quorum Court seats now held by Democrats—so the Republican members of the Quorum Court no longer hold a supermajority.  It may not sound like a big deal but in practical terms it makes a difference!}
}
